# The LEAN RUNTIME set. This is what the container image installs, and nothing else.
#
# Why this file exists, and why requirements.txt is NOT the lean one: the App Store's
# generated pipeline installs `requirements.txt` and then runs `pytest`. It does not know
# about a dev file, and the pipeline is generated so it cannot be edited to add one. A
# runtime-only requirements.txt therefore fails the Test stage with
# `pytest: command not found` and exit 127, which is exactly what happened on the first real
# upload: four of eight stages passed and Quality, Container Build and Container Scan were
# all skipped. The flight plan states this contract (requirements.txt carries the test
# tooling, requirements-runtime.txt stays lean) and it is now honoured.
#
# Policy (dependencies skill): no new runtime dependency without a recorded reason. The
# reasons live in requirements.in alongside the same pins, so there is one place to read them.
